            <ArticleTitle>Visualization of back pain data--a 3-D solution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>595-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Traditional approaches to gathering and visualizing pain data rely on two-dimensional (2-D) human body models, where different types of sensation are recorded with various monochrome symbols. We propose an alternative that uses a three-dimensional (3-D) representation of the human body, which can be marked in color to visualize and record pain data.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
